1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Every trading app gets paid when you lose.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,500
WinCut doesn't.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Drag the exit price below the entry.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:31,500
The fee stays at zero — and the loss is banked as a credit.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Only a profit is charged: 10% of it.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:47,500
Split trader 50 / referrer 20 / protocol 30.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Four markets on NEAR testnet.

8
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:04,500
Prices are live Ref Finance pool reserves, not a mock feed.

9
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:19,500
5-minute candles, built from the pool's own swaps.

10
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:30,000
A real buy, signed on testnet.

11
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:49,500
The contract holds the position. The wallet never does.

12
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Now a losing exit.

13
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Fee charged: 0.00

14
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:19,500
The loss became credit against the next win.

15
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:37,500
The same trade on the NEAR explorer. Nothing was taken.

16
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:46,000
343 settled trades. 97 losing exits. Zero fees on every one.

17
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:51,500
One fee ever charged: 0.076611 tUSDC — a tenth of a 0.77 profit.

18
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:56,000
The AI agent holds a key that can only buy and sell.

19
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:00,000
It cannot withdraw. Not by permission — by the key itself.
